# Signed documents embed a hash over their exact bytes, so their line
# endings must survive checkout unchanged on every platform.
*.sig -text

# Everything under test is byte sensitive for the same reason: the keys and
# document bodies the signatures are taken over, the compressed forms, and the
# expected outputs the harness compares byte for byte. The test plan in
# test/cases is ordinary JSON, but leaving its line endings alone costs
# nothing and keeps this to a single rule.
#
# Only -text, and not the binary macro, which would also unset diff. Blessing
# a golden and regenerating a fixture are both reviewed as diffs.
test/* -text
